<h2><%= l(:label_reporter_template_new) %></h2>

<%= labelled_form_for :template, @template,
                      url: project_reporter_templates_path(@project),
                      html: { method: :post, id: 'reporter-template-form' } do |f| %>
  <%= render partial: 'form', locals: { f: f } %>
  <p>
    <%= submit_tag l(:button_create) %>
    <%#
      PREVIEW BEFORE THE FIRST SAVE, which is when it is worth most: §9b.2's whole
      argument is that an author should find out at the keyboard that their template
      breaks in the PDF. Previewing only after saving would mean the first thing a new
      template does is get stored. Same mechanism as the editor's button, without an id —
      the content travels in the request and nothing is written.
    %>
    <%= submit_tag l(:label_preview),
                   name: 'preview',
                   formaction: preview_project_reporter_templates_path(@project),
                   formmethod: 'post' %>
    <%= link_to l(:button_cancel), project_reporter_templates_path(@project) %>
  </p>
<% end %>
